  "query_preview": "..Another quiet start to the afternoon convection\nwise with only a few CBs, as of 3 pm, over the eastern mountains.\nPWAT values range widely across the area this afternoon from \naround 1\" near the AZ/NM border to 2\" over far western Pima \ncounty. Main area of concern between 4-8 pm will be along or\nnear the Intl border of Santa Cruz and Cochise counties for \nstrong gusty winds and brief heavy rain.\n\nMonday: Not a whole lot of change in PWAT values from today. \nMain area of concern in the initial round of storms (some of \nwhich will be severe with heavy rain) will be along or near the\nIntl border from about San Miguel east to Douglas, with outflow\ninteractions spreading the threat of storms north. There is the\npotential for convection to develop during the overnight hours \ninto Tuesday morning.\n\nTuesday: At this time, models are suggesting that storm activity\nwill be mainly east and south of Tucson during the afternoon and\nevening hours.\n\nHighs Monday and Tuesday will run 3 to 5 degrees above normal.\n\nWednesday thru Sunday: Day-to-day variability of daily chances \nof showers and thunderstorms as the calender turns from July to\nAugust. Major HeatRisk returns to the area Thursday thru \nSaturday as highs heat back up to 8-10 degrees above normal. \nHeat products likely will be hoisted by later shifts.\n\n8-14 day outlooks (August 3-9)\nTemperature: Likely above normal (58-62% chance)\nPrecipitation: Likely above normal (49%-59% chance)",
